    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\cdot 0+(-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7})\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ 0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
